# Website Template export (WP / Squarespace)

Canonical plan: [`docs/audit/plan-2026-08-18-website-export-wp-squarespace.md`](../../docs/audit/plan-2026-08-18-website-export-wp-squarespace.md). Lessons: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-18-website-export.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-18-website-export.md). Data-driven WP theme (2026-09-26): `generateWordpressThemeZip` + `wordpress/build-php.ts`.

## As-built

GitHub Pages ZIP from `generateWebsiteZip()` is the **default** export. Classic WordPress theme ZIP from `generateWordpressThemeZip()` is a first-class second download: homepage copy is stored in a WordPress option, editable under **Appearance → Local site** (and Customizer), with JSON import of `unionops-website.json` for updates without a full theme re-upload.

**Layouts (2026-09):** curated `layoutId` values `solidarity` | `bulletin` | `hall` share one content model (`WebsiteTemplateData` / draft / `unionops-website.json` **v2**). Switching layouts never recreates copy. Multi-page site trees remain deferred — see [`docs/audit/website-template-world-class-2026-09.md`](../../docs/audit/website-template-world-class-2026-09.md).

Still not a CMS: no freeform block tree, no forms (`mailto:` only), no Squarespace export. Page copy persists in `WebsiteDraft` (localStorage) + Local Pack; hero photo bytes stay session-only. Both ZIPs include `unionops-website.json` so a steward can import the site file (or the ZIP) and regenerate. v1 JSON/ZIP imports migrate to v2 (`layoutId: solidarity`).

## Verdict

- **WordPress:** Supported as a classic PHP theme with in-WP content updates. UnionOps does **not** host WordPress or manage plugins/security on the steward’s server. Do not start with FSE / `theme.json`. WXR is still not a substitute.
- **Squarespace 7.1:** **non-option** for theme, developer-mode, or template ZIP. Do not scrape editor APIs. Do not advertise “Squarespace export.” Steward-facing copy: `/guide/website` Part 2 + `/tools/website-template` (`websiteGuide.squarespace`, `websiteTemplate.squarespaceNote`).

## Do not

- Replace GitHub Pages as the default export
- Promise a Squarespace-compatible template
- Invent a CMS/block tree solely to chase WP FSE or Squarespace Fluid Engine
- Fork a full HTML/CSS copy per layout — add layouts via the registry + section renderers
- Ship “UnionOps does not support WordPress” framing — distinguish **hosting** (not ours) from **theme + Local site updates** (supported)
